<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="i-theming">Theming</h2>
  <p>Everything is a CSS custom property — override inline or in your own
     stylesheet, no rebuild. <code>--_</code>-prefixed properties are internal
     state tokens and not part of the API.</p>
  <table class="docs-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Token</th><th>Affects</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-chip-h</code></td><td>Chip height (default 32px; the set's spacing keeps the 48px target)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-chip-radius</code></td><td>Shape — pill by default; <code>8px</code> gives the M3 boxy chip, <code>4px</code> Shrine-like, <code>0</code> a cut chip</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-accent</code></td><td>Selected text, check glyph, focus ring</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-tint</code></td><td>Selected fill</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-divider</code></td><td>Filled (unselected) container</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-border</code></td><td>Outlined container border, filled hover/active</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-hover</code></td><td>Outlined hover, disabled fill</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-disabled</code></td><td>Disabled text</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>--fl-icon-ph</code> / <code>--fl-text-secondary</code></td><td>Avatar fill and initials</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% set themeExample %}
:root {
  --fl-chip-radius: 8px;   /* M3's boxy chip — the pill is the M2 default */
  --fl-accent: #188038;    /* selection follows the brand */
  --fl-tint: #e6f4ea;
}
{% endset %}
  {{ snippet(themeExample) }}
  <p>The shape note is worth repeating: M2 chips are
     <strong>pills</strong> (16dp on 32dp) and Material 3 made them boxier
     with 8dp corners. Flint follows the M2 idiom and ships the radius as a
     token, so the M3 look is one line away.</p>
</section>
{% endset %}

